- Goal

Understand the difference between ASM and File System when creating:

- Datafiles
- Tablespaces
- Redo Logs
- Control Files

Same tasks… different storage approach.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

-> 1. Creating Tablespace

🔹 File System:

CREATE TABLESPACE app_data
DATAFILE '/u02/oradata/app_data01.dbf'
SIZE 500M;

🔹 ASM:

CREATE TABLESPACE app_data
DATAFILE '+DATA'
SIZE 500M;

📌 Difference:

- File System → you define exact file path
- ASM → Oracle decides file location automatically

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

-> 2. Adding Datafile

🔹 File System:

ALTER TABLESPACE app_data
ADD DATAFILE '/u02/oradata/app_data02.dbf'
SIZE 500M;

🔹 ASM:

ALTER TABLESPACE app_data
ADD DATAFILE '+DATA'
SIZE 500M;

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

-> 3. Redo Log Files

🔹 File System:

ALTER DATABASE ADD LOGFILE
('/u02/oradata/redo04.log') SIZE 200M;

🔹 ASM:

ALTER DATABASE ADD LOGFILE
('+DATA') SIZE 200M;

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

-> 4. Control Files

🔹 File System:

CONTROL_FILES='/u02/oradata/control01.ctl'

🔹 ASM:

CONTROL_FILES='+DATA'

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

-> Key Differences (Simple)

- File System:
 
 - Manual file paths
 - DBA controls everything
 - More responsibility

- ASM:
 
 - No file paths
 - Oracle manages storage
 - Auto balancing + better performance

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

💡 DBA Insight

If you see:
- “/u02/oradata/...” → File System
- “+DATA / +FRA” → ASM

That’s the fastest way to know the storage type.